1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,642
Movies picture gemstone mines

2
00:00:01,672 --> 00:00:03,338
as glittering crystal caves.

3
00:00:04,074 --> 00:00:05,594
In real underground mines,

4
00:00:05,651 --> 00:00:07,802
workers drill through solid grey rock.

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:09,304
Miners listen for the drill bit

6
00:00:09,334 --> 00:00:11,407
to suddenly drop into a hollow pocket.

7
00:00:12,152 --> 00:00:14,213
Inside, they don't find clean air—

8
00:00:14,321 --> 00:00:15,818
they hit sticky wet clay.

9
00:00:16,043 --> 00:00:17,193
Millions of years ago,

10
00:00:17,279 --> 00:00:18,846
superheated mineral fluids cooled

11
00:00:18,876 --> 00:00:20,869
inside sealed granite cavities.

12
00:00:21,623 --> 00:00:24,049
Thick pocket clay cushioned razor-sharp emeralds,

13
00:00:24,135 --> 00:00:26,252
tourmaline, and fluorite as they grew.

14
00:00:26,486 --> 00:00:28,687
Only after miners rinse away that grey mud

15
00:00:28,717 --> 00:00:30,934
do raw crystal faces flash with color.

16
00:00:31,687 --> 00:00:33,798
Yet above ground, jewelers slice out

17
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:35,896
cloudy specks as worthless flaws.

18
00:00:36,145 --> 00:00:37,570
To deep-Earth geologists,

19
00:00:37,654 --> 00:00:39,739
those rejected flaws are priceless.

20
00:00:40,484 --> 00:00:42,206
Some rough diamonds blast upward

21
00:00:42,236 --> 00:00:43,591
through volcanic pipes from more

22
00:00:43,621 --> 00:00:45,473
than 600 kilometers down.

23
00:00:45,692 --> 00:00:48,151
Firing X-ray beams into flawed diamonds,

24
00:00:48,249 --> 00:00:49,921
scientists found ringwoodite—

25
00:00:50,006 --> 00:00:51,876
a deep mineral locking away water.

26
00:00:52,629 --> 00:00:55,687
In 2018, diamonds even revealed Ice-Seven:

27
00:00:55,785 --> 00:00:57,655
solid high-pressure water ice.

28
00:00:57,895 --> 00:00:59,796
That doesn't mean an open underground ocean

29
00:00:59,826 --> 00:01:01,597
sloshes beneath Earth's crust.

30
00:01:02,378 --> 00:01:04,210
Most of that deep water stays trapped

31
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:07,235
inside crystal rock and microscopic fluid pockets.

32
00:01:07,523 --> 00:01:10,363
Jewelers polish away tiny inclusions for sparkle.

33
00:01:11,135 --> 00:01:13,491
Scientists read those same crystal traps

34
00:01:13,521 --> 00:01:14,669
as time capsules—

35
00:01:14,746 --> 00:01:16,715
carried up through solid mine rock.
